WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.383
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:10.047
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:16.389
Unit thirty-five: Nominalisation. Today you will turn verbs and adjectives into nouns for formal writing.

4
00:00:16.689 --> 00:00:19.388
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:23.729
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:26.177
Decide → decision.

7
00:00:27.183 --> 00:00:30.564
Decide → decision means a verb becoming a noun.

8
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.604
The decision was quick.

9
00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:36.937
Your turn. Say: Decide → decision.

10
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.183
Decide → decision.

11
00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.638
Fail → failure.

12
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.752
Fail → failure means a verb becoming a noun.

13
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.885
The failure was costly.

14
00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:54.937
Your turn. Say: Fail → failure.

15
00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.567
Fail → failure.

16
00:01:00.317 --> 00:01:02.363
Develop → development.

17
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.905
Develop → development means a verb becoming a noun.

18
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:08.796
Rapid development.

19
00:01:09.383 --> 00:01:12.663
Your turn. Say: Develop → development.

20
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.767
Develop → development.

21
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:19.599
Noun form.

22
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:23.163
Noun form means the noun version of a word.

23
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.366
The noun form of decide.

24
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.498
Your turn. Say: Noun form.

25
00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:32.485
Noun form.

26
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.518
Formal style.

27
00:01:35.517 --> 00:01:37.632
Formal style means serious writing.

28
00:01:38.217 --> 00:01:39.612
A formal style.

29
00:01:40.217 --> 00:01:43.299
Your turn. Say: Formal style.

30
00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:47.413
Formal style.

31
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.198
Abstract.

32
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:53.414
Abstract means an idea, not a physical thing.

33
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:55.494
An abstract noun.

34
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.445
Your turn. Say: Abstract.

35
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.440
Abstract.

36
00:02:03.183 --> 00:02:04.742
Information density.

37
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:09.746
Information density means how much information is in a text.

38
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.117
High information density.

39
00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:16.275
Your turn. Say: Information density.

40
00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.843
Information density.

41
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:22.619
Academic.

42
00:02:23.617 --> 00:02:26.359
Academic means related to study and research.

43
00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.346
Academic writing.

44
00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.869
Your turn. Say: Academic.

45
00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:35.758
Academic.

46
00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:40.647
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:45.352
Visal, rewrite: People are moving to cities quickly.

48
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:55.023
The rapid movement of people to cities. Nominalisation turns verbs and adjectives into nouns, so a whole idea fits in a noun phrase.

49
00:02:56.117 --> 00:02:57.617
What are examples?

50
00:02:58.717 --> 00:03:14.813
Decide → decision, fail → failure, develop → development, arrive → arrival, important → importance. The government decided quickly becomes the government's quick decision.

51
00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:16.964
Why use it?

52
00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:28.214
It makes writing more formal and more compact, because it packs a lot of information into fewer words. But too many abstract nouns make text hard to read.

53
00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.064
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:36.296
Grammar focus: Nominalisation: verb and adjective to noun.

55
00:03:36.596 --> 00:03:37.783
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:38.483 --> 00:03:41.957
The government decided quickly → the government's quick decision.

57
00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:46.545
People are moving to cities → the movement of people to cities.

58
00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.400
Technology developed → the development of technology.

59
00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:60.000
Turn verbs and adjectives into nouns (decide → decision). Use them for formal, dense academic style, but keep the balance.

60
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:04.679
Be careful! Don't say: People moved quick to cities.

61
00:04:06.633 --> 00:04:09.062
Say: The rapid movement to cities.

62
00:04:09.362 --> 00:04:10.851
Use a noun phrase.

63
00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:14.470
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:16.628
Verbs Become Nouns.

65
00:04:16.928 --> 00:04:21.040
The government decided quickly, and the decision surprised many people.

66
00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:26.401
People are moving to cities rapidly; this movement has changed society.

67
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.328
The development of technology has transformed work.

68
00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:34.018
Formal writing often uses abstract nouns.

69
00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.753
Too much nominalisation can make a text heavy.

70
00:04:38.867 --> 00:04:42.880
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:43.717 --> 00:04:45.658
fail → blank

72
00:04:45.958 --> 00:04:49.937
A, failing. B, failure. C, failed.

73
00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.383
The answer is B: failure.

74
00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:58.190
develop → blank

75
00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:02.491
A, development. B, developer. C, developing.

76
00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:08.312
The answer is A: development.

77
00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.252
important → blank

78
00:05:11.552 --> 00:05:15.635
A, importance. B, importantly. C, importanced.

79
00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.571
The answer is A: importance.

80
00:05:22.717 --> 00:05:24.124
Which is more formal?

81
00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:29.807
A, People decided quickly.. B, The decision was quick.. C, They decide fast..

82
00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:36.214
The answer is B: The decision was quick..

83
00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:40.731
According to the reading, what has changed society?

84
00:05:41.031 --> 00:05:45.729
A, movement to cities. B, a new law. C, the weather.

85
00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.754
The answer is A: movement to cities.

86
00:05:52.967 --> 00:05:56.281
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:57.117 --> 00:06:00.672
Rewrite 'People are moving to cities quickly' using a noun phrase.

88
00:06:09.483 --> 00:06:10.902
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:11.202 --> 00:06:22.005
The rapid movement of people to cities has increased pressure on housing. I changed the verb moving into the noun movement, and the adverb quickly into the adjective rapid.

90
00:06:22.305 --> 00:06:24.107
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:30.885
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and nominalisation: verb and adjective to noun.

92
00:06:31.185 --> 00:06:36.519
Today's value is intellectual rigor. Hold your ideas to the highest standard of evidence.

93
00:06:36.819 --> 00:06:39.622
See you in Unit thirty-six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:39.922 --> 00:06:42.935
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

